"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative focused on data analytics, cloud storage optimization, and secure file sharing. It was initially introduced with a kickoff scheduled for June 15th (or July 15th in one update) and led by Sarah Tan or Marcus Cole. The project received a budget increase from $500,000 to $2 million. Key developments include the addition of five new team members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, and planned UI enhancements in October. Security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption. Feedback was sought from stakeholders by the end of November, and a training budget of $15,000 was approved. The project is described as almost complete."
